{"availability":"available","full":"kikoncuo/jevfire","name":"jevfire","description":"JEV-inspired parallel decisions for CUDA LLMs. One context, many decisions. vLLM API, game-agent examples, and reproducible benchmarks.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":75,"forks":8,"created":"2026-09-16T14:45:51Z","updated":"2026-09-18T08:47:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kikoncuo.github.io/jevfire/learn.html","topics":["cuda","game-ai","inference","jev","llm","parallel-decoding","structured-output","vllm"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/harshatheg/Qwen-2.5-1B-RLCD","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2105759846247342377","postId":"2105759846247342377","postedAt":"2026-10-01T20:40:45.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T10:31:59.027Z","stars":75,"forks":8},{"at":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z","stars":75,"forks":8}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["JEVfire assigns typed variables from finite choices, batching independent fields through vLLM for parallel execution and reuse of their shared instruction/context prefix when the engine cache permits it. Inspired by JEV / RLCD, it uses the pretrained model's existing language-model head to score verified single-token labels, maps the winners to allowed values, and assembles JSON in code.","Traditional structured generation emits keys, punctuation, and values token by token. JEVfire maps each field's options to verified single-token labels, asks vLLM for their scores, and picks the best label for each field. Your application gets a JSON object without asking the model to spell it out.","vLLM owns CUDA execution and KV state. JEVfire is a lightweight HTTP sidecar; it does not load another copy of the model. Each field/chunk scores one output position. Engine scheduling can still require multiple batches and forward passes. Prompt layout, scoring, and differences from JEV / RLCD →"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kikoncuo/jevfire/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3440c5705062d46d092a5cae90e4ffa76fa7e7d90c3478ad3da9d143a9138b00","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T10:31:59.027Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"JEVfire assigns typed variables from finite choices, batching independent fields through vLLM for parallel execution and reuse of their shared instruction/context prefix when the engine cache permits it. Inspired by JEV / RLCD, it uses the pretrained model's existing language-model head to score verified single-token labels, maps the winners to allowed values, and assembles JSON in code.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kikoncuo/jevfire/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"New context still costs compute: longer prompts require prefill; cache reuse","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kikoncuo/jevfire/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"3440c5705062d46d092a5cae90e4ffa76fa7e7d90c3478ad3da9d143a9138b00","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kikoncuo/jevfire/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-18T08:47:45Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kikoncuo/jevfire/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T16:20:08.771Z","hash":"3440c5705062d46d092a5cae90e4ffa76fa7e7d90c3478ad3da9d143a9138b00","originalBytes":22658,"storedBytes":22658,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["model","json","docs","decisions","vllm","choices","fields","game","browser","context","jevfire","one","per","scores","boost","decision","python","action","benchmarks","cache","cuda","engine","independent","labels","local","prefix","qwen","race","through","appli